			<div class="content" id="post-content-4712912">
									

<p>Alright so I -1 this and I want to kinda talk about how I feel here. My big issue is that it just&#8230;feels disjointed? You've got a whole bunch of little narrative threads here (the initial body horror, the brief mention of two way communication with no indication of how it'd work, the kinda&#8230;story of what happens to the D-Class I guess, the resignation of O5-8); and they don't really like, naturally flow from one to the next so much as you shove them up and insist they're interesting facets of this; but none of them really have enough depth here to carry this.</p>
<p>I think it doesn't help that this feels like it's just, a very generic take on time travel? Like, it's Steins;Gate but with a loom instead of a microwave, and you don't really do much with it so I'm just like&#8230;'okay cool but so what? why does this matter?'. You like, kinda touch on this with the O5-8 stuff and the brief mention of two way communication; but neither is developed enough to carry this so it just feels&#8230;shallow.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;minor&nbsp;things</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>[This was despite images posted on their social media account showing them in an old mill].</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm, not sure why this is in square brackets?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It appears <span style="color: green">the</span> proximity of the strings on the loom <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">are</span><span style="color: green">is</span> dependant on <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">our</span><span style="color: green">the</span> deviation<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">s</span> from the other causal timelines.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think this reads better with my changes? It's just kinda an awkward sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This suggests that there would be a higher likelihood of any D-Class transferred across parallel timelines to once again become a D-class, same with doctors.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'a high likelihood that any&#8230;timelines would once again become a' would read better; the 'same with doctors' is just kinda awkwardly tacked on here: maybe using 'and the same with Foundation doctors' would read better? Maybe 'researchers' would be a better choice here too?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>05-8's body has been recovered yet</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You've relatively consistently used 0's instead of O's for the O5 members in the emails; and this specific bit is presumably missing a 'not'?</p>
