<p>Thanks for taking the time to reply Cyber!</p>
<p>The O5-8 point is meant to further show what happens when the loom strings cross and link back to the previous section. I shall have a rethink about how to better show that as it may be too convoluted with the sudden introduction of a different tangent. I couldn't find any mention of body horror in here though.</p>
<p>I have to be honest, I have heard of &quot;Steins;Gate&quot; but have no idea what actually it is. The loom itself is a reference to the &quot;Norns&quot; who are Norse weavers of fate; due to this being a piece of machinery I thought a loom would be the best choice as it weaves fabric. I may try expand those connections.</p>
<p>The two-way communication was meant to be sort of addressed by O5-8 getting lost in the other timeline, as well as the fact they have no reason to believe it goes to the same timeline every time.</p>
<p>I shall try drafting a few other concepts for the ending!</p>

