<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;FRAGILE MACHINERY. PROPERTY OF NORNS LLP&quot;<br />
During the investigation into his death, a single cut piece of silk thread was recovered from his body with the phrase &quot;Fate is a fickle mistress&quot; inked upon it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>IMO, I think you should cut these. I feel like these are giving the game away, as by making it less obvious that this is an artifact of the fates, the article would be better (or at least more subtle)… I’d keep in the bit about the women’s voices, that’s a good hint at what’s going on.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>showed a spike in hume levels, SCP-3326 was found to be the source</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Consider instead of hume levels, the loom giving off atemporal energy, like in some of Hammermaiden’s time travel series?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Further tests were proposed to figure out the limitations of SCP-3326.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like the tone isn’t very clinical… consider changing to “were proposed to ascertain the functional limitations of SCP-3326’s anomalous effects.”</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 02/09/2020, following an interview Junior Researcher Hawthorne carried out with D-38389-1 and D-38389-2, both of the D-Class broke free from their cells. D-473218-2 was noticed by a security guard when entering SCP-3326's containment chamber, but he was unable to prevent their entry into the room.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I am a little confused by this, as the first two D-class aren’t mentioned beyond the first sentence here.</p>
<p><em>Several times you mention that a sentence or longer message is printed on a strand of silk, and I just don’t understand how this would work. Strands are very narrow, way less than a centimeter.</em> Not sure how to fix this, but it takes me out of it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, this still isn't doing it for me. There are so many D-class that I lose focus on who we're focusing on each moment. Moreover, I still feel like the potential for exploration of time-paradox is untapped here. We have a device that when messed with changes the history of an individual, but the foundation is able to observe and compare their previous histories to that of their current. But right after establishing that, you go into the consequences of crossing the strands, and introduce the concept of alternate realities. But I feel like the first concept is the one to be explored.</p>
<p>I will say that this is better than the first iteration and will change to a no-vote.</p>

							</div>

								
